  "profile": {
    "video_id": "iron-snail:6n9t0SDne44",
    "purpose": "Compare four waxed canvas jackets (Huckberry, Bradley Mountain, Freenote Cloth and Rogue Territory) as the start of the creator's fall 'Waxed Jacket Olympics', covering specs, fit, standout traits, drawbacks and who each jacket suits.",
    "video_type": "comparison",
    "thesis": "Each of the four waxed jackets is run through the same format of base specs, sizing, 'accolades', cons and the stereotypical wearer. The video moves from the cheapest unlined Huckberry jacket up to the celebrity-famous Rogue Territory Supply Jacket.",
    "key_takeaways": [
      "Huckberry Waxed Trucker Jacket: $228, 7 oz Martexin-waxed sail cloth from Fairfield Textile Mills, unlined, generously cut, the cheapest jacket in the lineup.",
      "Bradley Mountain Cabin Jacket: 12 oz canvas, Japanese cotton flannel lining, eight front pockets, fly rod snap, leather D-ring tool tab, leather washers behind the buttons; cut burlier for layering; the creator fits an XS.",
      "Freenote Cloth Rider's Jacket: 10 oz Martexin-waxed fabric, flannel body lining with satin-lined sleeves, gusseted back with internal elastic bands; the creator fits a size small.",
      "Rogue Territory Supply Jacket in tan: 10 oz Indian fabric waxed by Martexin, unlined, the slimmest fit, worn by Daniel Craig as James Bond and by Ryan Reynolds.",
      "Martexin wax is used across all four jackets.",
      "Cons named: Bradley Mountain's short hem and lack of flat-felled seams; the Huckberry and Rogue Territory jackets have no lining.",
      "The creator is 5'9\" and 148 lb, which gives context for his sizing comments."
    ],
